{%- comment -%}
  The in-page purchase block: size, availability, Add to cart, Buy now.

  WHY THIS EXISTS
  Stage 2 moved buying to the sticky bar and dropped main-product's form, so
  the product page has had no working purchase control of its own — the theme's
  own Add to Cart still renders but is hidden by CSS in sections/main-product,
  and its [form="ProductForm-…"] target no longer exists. This puts the
  controls back on the page without reviving that dead form.

  HOW IT STAYS IN SYNC
  It renders as VariantPicker-{section}-{product}, which is exactly the id
  onrepeat-buy-bar already carries in data-picker. The bar was written expecting a
  picker there: choosing a chip calls echoToPicker(), which ticks the matching
  radio here and fires a bubbling change; choosing here fires the same event,
  which the bar's _onPickerChange listens for. Neither control owns the size —
  they mirror each other, so a shopper can use whichever is in front of them.

  WHY ITS OWN FORM
  Same reasoning the bar records for its own: action=/cart/add, is=product-form,
  a [name=id] and a [type=submit][name=add] is the three-element shape the
  theme's ProductForm class drives, which keeps AJAX cart, cart-drawer opening
  and error handling on the theme's tested path. {{ form | payment_button }}
  needs a real product form around it, which is also what makes Buy now
  possible here at all.

  Accepts:
  - product     {Object}  required
  - section_id  {String}  required, for unique ids
  - block       {Object}  optional, for shopify_attributes in the editor
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign bm_size_index = nil
  for opt in product.options_with_values
    assign opt_down = opt.name | downcase
    if opt_down contains 'size'
      assign bm_size_index = forloop.index0
      break
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Self-suppressing. The block is placed on every product template, but a gift
    card, a bundle or anything without a single size option has nothing for it
    to render — and a size picker with no sizes is worse than no picker. Those
    products keep the sticky bar exactly as before.

    The test lives in onrepeat-buy-module-active rather than here because
    main-product.liquid has to reach the same answer: it suppresses the
    shipping strip above the picker on exactly the products where this module
    renders its own copy below the buttons. One condition, one file.
  endcomment
  capture bm_active
    render 'onrepeat-buy-module-active', product: product
  endcapture
  assign bm_render = false
  if bm_active != blank and bm_size_index != nil
    assign bm_render = true
  endif

  assign bm_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign bm_form_id = 'OnRepeatBuyModuleForm-' | append: section_id | append: '-' | append: product.id
  assign bm_picker_id = 'VariantPicker-' | append: section_id | append: '-' | append: product.id

  comment
    Its own drawer id, for the reason the bar records: if two size-chart
    drawers ever exist, sharing an id puts two elements with the same id in the
    document and breaks whichever opener resolves second.
  endcomment
  assign bm_chart_page = settings.size_chart_page
  if bm_chart_page == blank
    assign bm_chart_page = pages['size-chart']
  endif
  assign bm_chart_modal_id = 'OnRepeatBuyModuleSizeChart-' | append: section_id | append: '-' | append: product.id
-%}

{%- if bm_render -%}
{%- capture bm_variants -%}[{%- for v in product.variants -%}{"id":{{ v.id }},"available":{{ v.available }},"option_value":{{ v.options[bm_size_index] | json }},"inventory_quantity":{% if v.inventory_management == 'shopify' and v.inventory_policy != 'continue' %}{{ v.inventory_quantity }}{% else %}null{% endif %}}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}]{%- endcapture -%}

<style>
  /* Scoped to the element so nothing here can reach the rest of the page.
     Everything is fluid: the size row is a wrapping grid rather than a fixed
     column count, so two sizes and nine sizes both look deliberate, and the
     action row collapses to one column only when two buttons genuinely stop
     fitting — measured, not guessed at a device width. */
  onrepeat-buy-module {
    display: block;
    margin: 18px 0 4px;
    container-type: inline-size;
  }
  .sbm__head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 9px;
  }
  .sbm__label {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #8b8079;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .sbm__label b {
    color: #1a1512;
    margin-left: 6px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .sbm__guide {
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: #5b524b;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 2px;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    cursor: pointer;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .sbm__guide:hover { color: #5c1011; }

  /* ── the size row ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
     One line, always. This used to be repeat(auto-fit, minmax(56px, 1fr)),
     which wraps the moment six sizes stop fitting a 56px floor — so a
     six-size tee showed five pills and a lonely XXL on a second row.

     grid-auto-flow: column with auto-columns of minmax(0, 1fr) states the
     rule directly: however many sizes arrive, they are columns of equal
     width. It needs no count, so it cannot fall out of step with the number
     of variants rendered. minmax's 0 floor is load-bearing — grid children
     default to min-width:auto, so "XXL" would otherwise push its track wider
     than its share and force the row past the container.

     Nothing has a fixed width any more, so the pill has to carry the fit
     itself; see .sbm__size span for the type and padding that do it.

     The fieldset is its own container so the cell arithmetic below can ask
     "how wide is this row" and get the row, not the block around it. --sbm-n
     is the only thing Liquid has to supply, and only the type reads it: get
     it wrong and the text is a little large or small, never wrapped. */
  .sbm__sizes {
    --sbm-gap: 7px;
    display: grid;
    grid-auto-flow: column;
    grid-auto-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--sbm-gap);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    min-width: 0;
    container-type: inline-size;
  }
  @container (max-width: 300px) {
    .sbm__sizes { --sbm-gap: 5px; }
  }
  .sbm__size { position: relative; display: block; min-width: 0; }
  /* The radio is hidden by clip-path, not by size or opacity alone. The theme
     styles every radio on the page with
       input:is([type="checkbox"],[type="radio"]):not(.switch) { width: 20px }
     which is (0,2,1) and outranked the (0,1,1) this used to be — so the
     "hidden" input kept its 20px width and its opacity, and painted a grey bar
     across the top-left corner of every pill. Matching that specificity would
     only win a tie on source order; clip-path removes the element from
     painting outright, whatever any other rule does to its box. It stays
     focusable, which is what the ring on the sibling span depends on. */
  .sbm .sbm__size input {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    opacity: 0;
    appearance: none;
    -webkit-appearance: none;
    background: none;
    clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    overflow: hidden;
    white-space: nowrap;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  /* --sbm-cell is the exact width one pill gets: the row minus the gaps,
     divided by the number of pills. It is declared HERE rather than on the
     row because a custom property resolves its units where it is used —
     100cqw asked from inside a pill means the fieldset (the nearest
     container), which is the width we actually want; asked from the fieldset
     itself it would mean the block around it.

     0.30 of the cell keeps "XXL" comfortably inside its pill, and the clamp
     stops there: 15px is the size the row has always used and the ceiling for
     three sizes on a desktop column, 10.5px the floor where six sizes still
     read cleanly at 320px. Past the floor the ellipsis takes over rather than
     the row breaking — a shrunken label is recoverable, a wrapped row is the
     bug being fixed. */
  .sbm__size span {
    --sbm-cell: calc((100cqw - (var(--sbm-n, 6) - 1) * var(--sbm-gap)) / var(--sbm-n, 6));
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 46px;
    padding: 10px clamp(2px, calc(var(--sbm-cell) * 0.08), 8px);
    border: 1px solid #ddd6ce;
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: #fff;
    color: #1a1512;
    font-size: clamp(10.5px, calc(var(--sbm-cell) * 0.3), 15px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1;
    cursor: pointer;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
    transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .sbm__size:hover input:not(:disabled) + span { border-color: #b3a89f; }
  .sbm__size input:checked + span {
    background: #1a1512;
    border-color: #1a1512;
    color: #fff;
  }
  /* Focus lives on the hidden input, so the ring has to be drawn on the label
     it controls or keyboard users get nothing. */
  .sbm__size input:focus-visible + span {
    outline: 2px solid #5c1011;
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .sbm__size input:disabled + span {
    color: #c3bbb3;
    background: #faf8f6;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  .sbm__size input:disabled + span::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: linear-gradient(to top right, transparent calc(50% - 0.6px), #e3d5d5 50%, transparent calc(50% + 0.6px));
  }
  .sbm__dot {
    position: absolute;
    top: 5px;
    right: 6px;
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #b4740f;
  }
  .sbm__size input:checked + span .sbm__dot { background: #ffb74d; }
  .sbm__size input:disabled + span .sbm__dot { display: none; }

  /* Reserved height so choosing a size does not shunt the buttons down the
     page under the shopper's thumb. */
  .sbm__stock {
    min-height: 18px;
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: #8b8079;
  }
  .sbm__stock b { font-weight: 600; }
  .sbm__stock[data-tone="low"] { color: #b4740f; }
  .sbm__stock[data-tone="ok"] { color: #2f6b4f; }

  .sbm__actions {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 9px;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  /* Container query, not a viewport media query: this block sits in a column
     whose width does not track the viewport — it is full-bleed on a phone and
     roughly half the page on a desktop PDP. Asking how wide THIS element is, is
     the only question whose answer is always right. */
  @container (max-width: 340px) {
    .sbm__actions { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  @supports not (container-type: inline-size) {
    @media (max-width: 380px) {
      .sbm__actions { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
    /* Without container queries cqw is not a length, so --sbm-cell resolves to
       nothing and takes the whole clamp() with it — an invalid font-size falls
       back to inherited body type, which is worse than any fixed value. Pin
       both properties to the sizes that hold six pills on the narrowest phone
       we support. The row itself is unaffected: grid-auto-flow needs no query. */
    .sbm__size span {
      font-size: 12.5px;
      padding: 10px 3px;
    }
    @media (min-width: 481px) {
      .sbm__size span { font-size: 15px; padding: 10px 6px; }
    }
  }

  .sbm__btn {
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    min-height: 48px;
    padding: 13px 12px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 7px;
    width: 100%;
    text-align: center;
    transition: background 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease, transform 0.12s ease;
  }
  .sbm__btn:active { transform: scale(0.985); }
  .sbm__btn:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #5c1011; outline-offset: 2px; }
  .sbm__btn--atc {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #fff;
    border-color: #1a1512;
    color: #1a1512;
  }
  .sbm__btn--atc:hover { background: #f5f2ef; }

  /* ── the add in flight ──────────────────────────────────────────────
     The same three states, colours and marks the sticky bar's CTA uses, so a
     shopper who taps one and then the other sees one behaviour rather than
     two. The bar owns the canonical version in onrepeat-buy-bar.liquid; this is
     deliberately a mirror of it and the two are meant to be read together.

     The theme's own ProductForm does set aria-busy on this button and animate
     a dot loader inside it — but only inside a .btn-text span this button
     does not have, so the whole response to a tap was nothing at all for the
     ~1.7s two sequential requests take. */
  .sbm__ico { display: flex; flex: 0 0 auto; }
  .sbm__ico:empty { display: none; }
  .sbm__btn--atc[data-cta='busy'],
  .sbm__btn--atc[data-cta='busy']:hover {
    background: #6e2122;
    border-color: #6e2122;
    color: #fff;
    cursor: progress;
  }
  .sbm__btn--atc[data-cta='done'],
  .sbm__btn--atc[data-cta='done']:hover {
    background: #2f6b4f;
    border-color: #2f6b4f;
    color: #fff;
    cursor: default;
  }
  .sbm__spin {
    display: block;
    width: 15px;
    height: 15px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 2px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35);
    border-top-color: #fff;
    animation: sbm-spin 0.6s linear infinite;
  }
  @keyframes sbm-spin {
    to { transform: rotate(360deg); }
  }
  .sbm__tick { display: block; width: 15px; height: 15px; }
  .sbm__tick path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: #fff;
    stroke-width: 2.6;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
    stroke-dasharray: 22;
    stroke-dashoffset: 22;
    animation: sbm-draw 0.28s ease forwards;
  }
  @keyframes sbm-draw {
    to { stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
  }
  /* A second signal, in case the button is under the thumb that just tapped
     it. It rides the button's own bottom edge rather than the block's top, so
     it cannot be mistaken for the page loading. */
  .sbm__prog {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    height: 2px;
    overflow: hidden;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .sbm__btn--atc[data-cta='busy'] .sbm__prog { opacity: 1; }
  .sbm__prog i {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    width: 36%;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
    animation: sbm-slide 1s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  @keyframes sbm-slide {
    0% { transform: translateX(-100%); }
    100% { transform: translateX(320%); }
  }
  /* While the add is in flight the size cannot change under it. */
  .sbm[data-adding] .sbm__size { pointer-events: none; opacity: 0.55; }
  .sbm[data-adding] .sbm__buy { pointer-events: none; opacity: 0.55; }

  .sbm__err {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: #9d2b28;
  }

  /* Before a size is chosen the block shows ONE live button, not two dead
     ones. A disabled control explains nothing and cannot be tapped to find out
     why; this one is tappable and points at what is missing. */
  .sbm[data-state="unset"] .sbm__actions { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .sbm[data-state="unset"] .sbm__buy { display: none; }
  .sbm[data-state="unset"] .sbm__btn--atc {
    background: #efedea;
    border-color: #e0dad3;
    color: #8b8079;
  }
  .sbm[data-state="soldout"] .sbm__actions { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .sbm[data-state="soldout"] .sbm__buy { display: none; }
  /* No accelerated checkout on the shop: Add to cart takes the whole row. */
  .sbm--nobuy .sbm__actions { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }

  @keyframes sbm-nudge {
    0%, 100% { transform: translateX(0); }
    25% { transform: translateX(-4px); }
    75% { transform: translateX(4px); }
  }
  .sbm__sizes.is-asking { animation: sbm-nudge 0.32s ease; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .sbm__sizes.is-asking { animation: none; }
    .sbm__btn, .sbm__size span { transition: none; }
    /* The spinner still has to read as "working", so it steps rather than
       sweeps instead of disappearing entirely. */
    .sbm__spin { animation-duration: 1.2s; animation-timing-function: steps(8, end); }
    .sbm__tick path { animation: none; stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
    .sbm__prog i { animation: none; width: 100%; opacity: 0.5; }
  }

  /* Shopify renders the dynamic checkout button itself, so it is styled to
     match rather than rebuilt — its internals are not ours to author. */
  .sbm__buy { display: block; min-height: 48px; }
  /* Shopify's button ships its own colour, and the theme's reset sends
     `color: inherit` down every button — so setting only the background left
     black text on maroon. Both class variants are named because the unbranded
     one is what renders once Shopify's script has run. */
  .sbm__buy .shopify-payment-button__button,
  .sbm__buy .shopify-payment-button__button--unbranded {
    border-radius: 10px !important;
    min-height: 48px !important;
    font-size: 14px !important;
    font-weight: 600 !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em !important;
    color: #fff !important;
    background: #780E09 !important;
    border: 0 !important;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 10px rgba(120, 16, 9, 0.22) !important;
    transition: background 0.15s ease !important;
  }
  .sbm__buy .shopify-payment-button__button:hover,
  .sbm__buy .shopify-payment-button__button--unbranded:hover:not([disabled]) {
    background: #8f120c !important;
    color: #fff !important;
  }
  /* Shopify paints a spinner into this pseudo-element while the order is being
     staged; left at the inherited colour it is invisible on the maroon. */
  .sbm__buy .shopify-payment-button__button[aria-busy="true"] { color: #fff !important; }
  .sbm__buy .shopify-payment-button__more-options { display: none !important; }

  /* ── Buy 2 Get 1 strip ──────────────────────────────────────────────
     One line between the stock line and the buttons — read at the exact
     moment the shopper decides how many. Gold border on a 7% gold wash so it
     reads as the offer family (the ship strip below uses the same gold), with
     the crimson chip carrying the offer name. Gated through onrepeat-b2g1-on,
     so the live theme renders nothing until go-live. */
  .sbm__offer {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
    margin-top: 12px;
    padding: 9px 11px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(202, 161, 90, 0.55);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(202, 161, 90, 0.07), rgba(202, 161, 90, 0.07)), #fff;
  }
  .sbm__offer-tag {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    font-size: 9.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    line-height: 1;
    color: #fff;
    background: #5c1011;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 5px 7px;
  }
  .sbm__offer-txt {
    min-width: 0;
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: #1a1512;
  }
  .sbm__offer-txt b { font-weight: 600; }

  /* Only the placement is ours; every colour, size and rule comes from
     .onrepeat-ship-strip so the two strips stay identical by construction.
     The strip already carries margin: 8px 0, so this just sets the gap from
     the buttons above it. */
  .sbm__strip { margin-top: 14px; }
  /* Three short labels, so they hold one line far below the width the
     reference strip survives at. The floor is the same 9px it steps down to. */
  @container (max-width: 330px) {
    .sbm__strip .onrepeat-ship-strip__val { font-size: 9px; }
    .sbm__strip .onrepeat-ship-strip__col { gap: 4px; }
  }
</style>

<onrepeat-buy-module
  class="sbm"
  data-state="unset"
  data-variants='{{ bm_variants | strip_newlines | escape }}'
  {% if block %}{{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}
>
  {%- form 'product', product, id: bm_form_id, is: 'product-form', data-hide-errors: 'true', class: 'sbm__form' -%}
    <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ bm_variant.id }}" data-sbm-vid>
    <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">

    <div class="sbm__head">
      <p class="sbm__label">Size<b data-sbm-chosen></b></p>
      {%- if bm_chart_page != blank -%}
        <button type="button" class="sbm__guide" aria-controls="{{ bm_chart_modal_id }}" aria-expanded="false">Size guide</button>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      id is the contract with onrepeat-buy-bar's data-picker. Renamed and the two
      controls stop mirroring each other, silently.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      --sbm-n is the pill count, and only the type scale reads it — the row is
      laid out by grid-auto-flow, which counts for itself. Every variant is
      rendered, sold out ones included, so the count is the variant count.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <fieldset class="sbm__sizes" id="{{ bm_picker_id }}" data-sbm-sizes style="--sbm-n: {{ product.variants.size }}">
      <legend class="sr-only">Choose a size</legend>
      {%- for v in product.variants -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign v_value = v.options[bm_size_index]
          assign v_qty = nil
          if v.inventory_management == 'shopify' and v.inventory_policy != 'continue'
            assign v_qty = v.inventory_quantity
          endif
        -%}
        <label class="sbm__size">
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="sbm-size-{{ section_id }}-{{ product.id }}"
            value="{{ v_value | escape }}"
            data-variant-id="{{ v.id }}"
            {% unless v.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
          >
          <span>
            {{- v_value -}}
            {%- if v.available and v_qty != nil and v_qty > 0 and v_qty <= 2 -%}
              <i class="sbm__dot" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </label>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </fieldset>

    {%- comment -%}
      A live region, so the availability that appears on choosing a size is
      actually announced rather than only drawn.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="sbm__stock" data-sbm-stock role="status" aria-live="polite">Select a size to see availability</p>

    {%- capture bm_b2g1 -%}{%- render 'onrepeat-b2g1-on' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if bm_b2g1 != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Placed inside the module rather than as its own block so it appears on
        all 8 product templates automatically and disappears with the module on
        products where it self-suppresses — an offer chip on a gift card would
        be a lie. One line and no caveat: the strip names the offer, and the
        cart ladder carries the tier walk and the amounts, where the shopper
        is actually deciding how many.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="sbm__offer">
        <span class="sbm__offer-tag" aria-hidden="true">B2G1</span>
        {%- comment -%}
          One line, no microcopy. The strip names the offer; the tier walk
          lives where the decision is made — the cart ladder.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="sbm__offer-txt"><b>Buy any 2, get the 3rd free</b></span>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="sbm__actions">
      {%- comment -%}
        The icon slot and the progress rail are permanent children, not markup
        the state machine writes and rewrites. Only the slot's contents change,
        so nothing holding a reference to the label or the rail can have it
        pulled out from under it mid-flight.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button type="submit" name="add" class="sbm__btn sbm__btn--atc" data-sbm-add>
        <span class="sbm__ico" data-sbm-add-ico aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span data-sbm-add-text>Select a size</span>
        <span class="sbm__prog" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
      </button>
      <div class="sbm__buy" data-sbm-buy>
        {{ form | payment_button }}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      The stock line above is already a live region, but it belongs to the size,
      not to the add — announcing "Adding…" there would wipe "Only 1 left in L"
      and never put it back. This is the add's own channel.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="sr-only" data-sbm-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
    <p class="sbm__err" data-sbm-err hidden></p>
  {%- endform -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Reuses .onrepeat-ship-strip rather than restyling a private copy. That class is
    defined in sections/main-product.liquid, the same section this block renders
    inside, so it is always present — and reusing it is the only way the two
    strips on the page cannot drift apart when one is edited. Only the icons and
    the three labels are ours.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="onrepeat-ship-strip sbm__strip">
    <div class="onrepeat-ship-strip__col">
      <span class="onrepeat-ship-strip__chip"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg></span>
      <span class="onrepeat-ship-strip__val">Secure payment</span>
    </div>
    <div class="onrepeat-ship-strip__col">
      {%- comment -%} The same path the shipping strip uses, so the two read as one system. {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="onrepeat-ship-strip__chip"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="17 1 21 5 17 9"/><path d="M3 11V9a4 4 0 0 1 4-4h14"/><polyline points="7 23 3 19 7 15"/><path d="M21 13v2a4 4 0 0 1-4 4H3"/></svg></span>
      <span class="onrepeat-ship-strip__val">7-day exchange</span>
    </div>
    <div class="onrepeat-ship-strip__col">
      <span class="onrepeat-ship-strip__chip"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></span>
      <span class="onrepeat-ship-strip__val">Ships in 24 hrs</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</onrepeat-buy-module>

{%- if bm_chart_page != blank -%}
  {%- render 'size-chart-modal',
      modal_id: bm_chart_modal_id,
      product: product,
      chart_page: bm_chart_page,
      title: bm_chart_page.title | default: 'Size chart' -%}
{%- endif -%}

<script>
  (function () {
    if (customElements.get('onrepeat-buy-module')) return;

    class OnRepeatBuyModule extends HTMLElement {
      connectedCallback() {
        try { this.variants = JSON.parse(this.dataset.variants || '[]'); }
        catch (e) { this.variants = []; }

        this.vid      = this.querySelector('[data-sbm-vid]');
        this.sizesEl  = this.querySelector('[data-sbm-sizes]');
        this.stockEl  = this.querySelector('[data-sbm-stock]');
        this.chosenEl = this.querySelector('[data-sbm-chosen]');
        this.addText  = this.querySelector('[data-sbm-add-text]');
        this.addIco   = this.querySelector('[data-sbm-add-ico]');
        this.addBtn   = this.querySelector('[data-sbm-add]');
        this.statusEl = this.querySelector('[data-sbm-status]');
        this.errEl    = this.querySelector('[data-sbm-err]');
        this.formEl   = this.querySelector('form');

        // Delegated, and listening for `change` rather than click: the sticky
        // bar mirrors a choice by ticking a radio and firing change, so a click
        // handler would miss everything the bar does.
        this._onChange = (e) => {
          const r = e.target;
          if (!r || r.type !== 'radio') return;
          this.select(r.value);
        };
        this.addEventListener('change', this._onChange);

        // The un-set button is live on purpose; it points at the size row.
        this._onAdd = (e) => {
          if (this.adding) { e.preventDefault(); return; }
          if (this.dataset.state !== 'unset') return;
          e.preventDefault();
          this.ask();
        };
        if (this.addBtn) this.addBtn.addEventListener('click', this._onAdd);

        // Listening for submit rather than the click: the theme's ProductForm
        // is what actually performs the add, and submit is the one signal that
        // fires however it was reached — pointer, Enter on the button, or a
        // requestSubmit from anywhere else. Its own handler preventDefaults and
        // takes over from here; ours only drives what the button looks like.
        this._onSubmit = () => {
          if (this.dataset.state === 'ready') this.begin();
        };
        if (this.formEl) this.formEl.addEventListener('submit', this._onSubmit);

        // {{ form | payment_button }} renders nothing when the shop has no
        // accelerated checkout enabled. Left alone that is an empty 48px gap
        // beside Add to cart, so the column is dropped instead and the button
        // goes full width — the same shape the un-set state already uses.
        const buy = this.querySelector('[data-sbm-buy]');
        if (buy && !buy.querySelector('button, [role="button"], iframe')) {
          buy.remove();
          this.classList.add('sbm--nobuy');
        }

        // A pre-selected variant (?variant= in the URL) should arrive chosen.
        const pre = this.querySelector('input[type="radio"]:checked');
        if (pre) this.select(pre.value);
        else this.paint(null);
      }

      disconnectedCallback() {
        this.removeEventListener('change', this._onChange);
        if (this.addBtn) this.addBtn.removeEventListener('click', this._onAdd);
        if (this.formEl) this.formEl.removeEventListener('submit', this._onSubmit);
        // An add in flight holds two document listeners and two timers; leaving
        // either behind would let a detached element answer a later add.
        this.settle(false, null, true);
      }

      byValue(v) {
        return this.variants.filter((x) => x.option_value === v)[0] || null;
      }

      select(value) {
        const v = this.byValue(value);
        if (!v) return;
        const radio = Array.prototype.slice
          .call(this.querySelectorAll('input[type="radio"]'))
          .filter((r) => r.value === value)[0];
        if (radio && !radio.checked) radio.checked = true;
        if (this.vid) this.vid.value = v.id;
        this.paint(v);
      }

      paint(v) {
        // A new size is a new attempt; the previous failure no longer applies.
        // The live region is emptied along with it, or a second failure with
        // the same wording would leave its text unchanged and go unannounced.
        this.showErr('');
        this.say('');
        if (!v) {
          this.dataset.state = 'unset';
          if (this.chosenEl) this.chosenEl.textContent = '';
          if (this.stockEl) {
            this.stockEl.removeAttribute('data-tone');
            this.stockEl.textContent = 'Select a size to see availability';
          }
          this.setCta('Select a size', '');
          return;
        }
        if (this.chosenEl) this.chosenEl.textContent = ' ' + v.option_value;

        if (!v.available) {
          this.dataset.state = 'soldout';
          if (this.stockEl) {
            this.stockEl.removeAttribute('data-tone');
            this.stockEl.textContent = 'Sold out in ' + v.option_value;
          }
          this.setCta('Sold out', '');
          if (this.addBtn) this.addBtn.disabled = true;
          return;
        }

        this.dataset.state = 'ready';
        if (this.addBtn) this.addBtn.disabled = false;
        this.setCta('Add to cart', '');
        if (this.stockEl) {
          const q = v.inventory_quantity;
          if (q != null && q > 0 && q <= 2) {
            this.stockEl.setAttribute('data-tone', 'low');
            this.stockEl.innerHTML = 'Only <b>' + q + ' left</b> in ' + v.option_value;
          } else {
            this.stockEl.setAttribute('data-tone', 'ok');
            this.stockEl.textContent = 'In stock';
          }
        }
      }

      // ── the button's visible state ───────────────────────────────────
      // The label always names what is happening, and the mark carries it for
      // anyone who does not read the label. data-cta is only ever set for the
      // two transient states, so the resting look stays governed by the host's
      // data-state and there is one source of truth per state.
      setCta(label, icon) {
        if (!this.addBtn) return;
        // An add in flight owns the button until it settles — a variant
        // re-render must not wipe the spinner out from under it.
        if (this.adding && icon !== 'spin') return;
        if (icon === 'spin' || icon === 'tick') {
          this.addBtn.dataset.cta = icon === 'spin' ? 'busy' : 'done';
        } else {
          delete this.addBtn.dataset.cta;
        }
        if (this.addIco) {
          this.addIco.innerHTML =
            icon === 'spin' ? '<span class="sbm__spin"></span>'
            : icon === 'tick' ? '<svg class="sbm__tick" viewBox="0 0 24 24" focusable="false"><path d="M4 12.5l5.2 5.2L20 7"/></svg>'
            : '';
        }
        if (this.addText) this.addText.textContent = label;
      }

      say(msg) {
        if (this.statusEl) this.statusEl.textContent = msg;
      }

      showErr(msg) {
        if (!this.errEl) return;
        this.errEl.textContent = msg || '';
        this.errEl.hidden = !msg;
      }

      // The theme's ProductForm does the add; this only tracks it. It answers
      // to the two document events the theme dispatches, bound for the life of
      // one submit so another surface's add can never drive this button.
      begin() {
        if (this.adding) return;
        this.adding = true;
        this.dataset.adding = '';
        this.showErr('');
        window.clearTimeout(this._doneTimer);
        this.setCta('Adding', 'spin');
        this.say('Adding ' + (this.chosenEl ? this.chosenEl.textContent.trim() : '') + ' to your bag');

        this._onAdded = () => this.settle(true);
        this._onErr = (e) => this.settle(false, e && e.detail && e.detail.errorMessage);
        document.addEventListener('ajaxProduct:added', this._onAdded);
        document.addEventListener('ajaxProduct:error', this._onErr);
        // If the network never answers, the button must not stay stuck.
        this._addTimer = window.setTimeout(
          () => this.settle(false, 'That took too long. Please try again.'),
          15000
        );
      }

      // quiet: tear the listeners and timers down without touching the DOM,
      // for the case where the element is going away.
      settle(ok, msg, quiet) {
        if (!this.adding) return;
        this.adding = false;
        window.clearTimeout(this._addTimer);
        document.removeEventListener('ajaxProduct:added', this._onAdded);
        document.removeEventListener('ajaxProduct:error', this._onErr);
        if (quiet) return;
        delete this.dataset.adding;

        if (!ok) {
          this.setCta('Add to cart', '');
          this.showErr(msg || 'Could not add that. Please try again.');
          this.say(msg || 'Could not add that item');
          return;
        }

        // Held, not flashed: the cart drawer is opening over this, and a
        // confirmation nobody sees is the problem we started with.
        this.setCta('Added', 'tick');
        this.say('Added to your bag');
        this._doneTimer = window.setTimeout(() => {
          if (this.adding) return;
          if (this.dataset.state === 'ready') this.setCta('Add to cart', '');
        }, 1100);
      }

      ask() {
        if (!this.sizesEl) return;
        this.sizesEl.classList.remove('is-asking');
        void this.sizesEl.offsetWidth;
        this.sizesEl.classList.add('is-asking');
        const first = this.querySelector('input[type="radio"]:not(:disabled)');
        if (first) first.focus();
        window.setTimeout(() => this.sizesEl.classList.remove('is-asking'), 700);
      }
    }

    customElements.define('onrepeat-buy-module', OnRepeatBuyModule);
  })();
</script>
{%- endif -%}
